\par\par \b \uc2 Short Sellers Shudder at Alibaba's Share Surge\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gregor Stuart Hunter \par \uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2017\par 02:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 It's been an expensive year to bet against China.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI China index, which consists of Chinese stocks listed on overseas markets, is up around 48% year-to-date, the strongest performance of any country benchmark that the global index company tracks. China's tech giants in particular have been on a tear, led by New York-listed Alibaba Group Holding and Hong Kong-listed Tencent Holdings .\par \par \uc2 The result has been painful for investors attempting to short China. Short-selling involves borrowing shares to sell, returning them at a later date. If the price falls in the interim, an investor can make a profit. But if the share price rises, a short seller can face unlimited losses.\par \par \uc2 To see just how painful this can be, take a look at Alibaba, the most-shorted Chinese stock.\par \par \uc2 Short interest in the e-commerce giant -- the amount of stocks that investors have loaned out for short-selling purposes -- totals $23.3 billion, according to data from S3 Partners, equivalent to more than 5% of its freely traded market value as of Friday's close. With the stock up 108% since the start of the year, S3 estimates that short sellers have been left with estimated mark-to-market losses of $12.2 billion in aggregate.\par \par \uc2 In the Hong Kong market, \uc2 Ping An Insurance\uc2  (Group) is the most-shorted stock, with $13.3 billion in short interest. Yet the stock is still up 82% this year, leading to mark-to-market losses of $3.9 billion, S3 estimates.\par \par \uc2 Next is internet gaming and social-media giant \uc2 Tencent Holdings Ltd\uc2 , which has $5.1 billion in short interest. That stock is up 94% this year, creating mark-to-market losses of $2.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 Other painful shorts include \uc2 China Evergrande Group\uc2  and \uc2 Sunac China Holdings\uc2 , two highly leveraged real-estate developers whose share prices have soared this year.\par \par \uc2 It hasn't all been bad news for short sellers. The most profitable short was \uc2 China Huishan Dairy Holdings\uc2 , whose share price suddenly collapsed in March this year. It later transpired that the company's accounts had overstated its cash position, after an executive director who jointly controlled much of the company's stock and was in charge of much of the company's affairs went missing.\par \par \uc2 The stock had been targeted by short seller Muddy Waters the previous year, which alleged fraud at the company. Year-to-date profits for those shorting Huishan total $139.7 million, according to S3's calculations.\par \par \uc2 Shorting stocks like Alibaba is a popular move with hedge funds seeking a liquid proxy for the Chinese consumer economy. It doesn't always reflect an expectation that a company will encounter difficulty: Some hedge fund strategies may go short on a particular Chinese company as a hedge on another investment elsewhere in the global economy.\par \par \uc2 The popularity of Chinese tech firms as shorting tools also reflects a lack of viable alternatives for anyone wanting to bet against China Inc. In theory, foreigners can short Chinese shares listed on the country's own stock exchanges via a trading link with Hong Kong. But there is a design flaw in the trading link's mechanism that means that no such trades have been recorded in the two years since it launched.\par \par \uc2 It has also proved hard to short China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan, which is traded offshore in places like \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on several occasions to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever speculators' negative yuan bets have started to mount.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 07-11-17 0132GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020171107edb70000z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
