\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar outlook bearish despite big rally\b0\par\par\uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2017\par 10:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sept 14 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar has retreated from its sharp rally last week triggered by the yuan\u8217\'20\'19s rise and broad weakness in the U.S. dollar, but analysts expect low interest rates will keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the weaker side of its narrow trading band.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar spot rate was marginally firmer against the dollar at 7.8116 by 0758 GMT on Thursday, and is on track to finish the week slightly higher, preserving all of its gains from last week.\par \par \uc2 The pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied sharply and unexpectedly against the dollar on Friday, when it tore through the crucial 7.8 level to the higher side of its 7.75 to 7.85 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band after steadily depreciating against the dollar all of this year.\par \par \uc2 It rallied 0.17 percent over Wednesday to Friday last week, after having declined about 0.9 percent in previous eight months.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said they expected the Hong Kong dollar to remain weak, primarily because of a widening interest rate differential as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  progresses with rate rises.\par \par \uc2 It has raised rates twice this year and is expected to reveal next week its plans for unwinding massive fiscal stimulus introduced after the financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt (the U.S. dollar-HK dollar value) still should go higher because of the onshore rates are still very low, relative to the U.S. rates," said Andy Ji, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It doesn't matter how gradually the U.S. is tightening monetary policy. For Hong Kong, liquidity is too flush. There is no way it can soak up enough liquidity, so that's the main driver for the Hong Kong dollar,\u8221\'20\'1D Ji added.\par \par \uc2 The sum of balances maintained by commercial banks with the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), also called the 'aggregate balance', was HK$227.54 billion ($29.13 billion) as of Wednesday's close, a notable drop from end-August.\par \par \uc2 It had beene as high as HK$426.34 billion in late 2015, but has been steady around the HK$260 billion level in the past 12 months.\par \par \uc2 HIBOR-LIBOR spreads, the differential between floating rates at which banks lend to each other in Hong Kong and the U.S. respectively, have been gradually widening since 2015, and the 3-month spread is now 0.56536 versus -0.02878 basis points at the beginning of this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast week\u8217\'20\'19s rally happened mainly because of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting a day before -- no one knew what would happen, everyone was long euro. Also, there was the North Korea threat,\u8221\'20\'1D a trader said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe market was long U.S. dollar against the Hong Kong dollar. If North Korea launched a missile over the weekend, the dollar could further fall. So the market unwound its previous dollar position.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the end of last week, the dollar was at its weakest in more than 2-1/2 years against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the euro jumped after a Reuters report showed that \uc2 ECB\uc2  policymakers were in broad agreement that their potential next step would be to reduce their bond purchases.\par \par \uc2 Dollar bearishness was exacerbated by fears North Korea may test fire another missile over the weekend, Hurricane Irma sweeping the western coast of the United States of America, and reduced expectations of another rate hike by the U.S. Federal reserve this year.\par \par \uc2 Broad dollar weakness forced the unwinding of long dollar positions across \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the yuan blowing past the 6.5 per dollar level.\par \par \uc2 The yuan's rally onshore was echoed by sharp gains in the offshore yuan -- which touched its highest since March 16 -- and the Hong Kong dollar.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sensitivity of the USD-HKD to the USD-CNY picked up as the latter broke the 6.5 level,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wee Choon Teo, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, Asia ex-Japan, at Nomura.\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe widening spreads and ample cash in the Hong Kong dollar market, compounded by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  constrained by policy choices, will keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mired in the weaker end of the trading band.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still far from levels that would spur any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey (HKMA) are not in a market to influence the interest rates. So, any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in terms of liquidity withdrawal is going to be very minimal. That is until it hits the top of the band and they are forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Till then they just wait and watch and hope the U.S. doesn't raise rates faster than expected,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ji.\par \par \uc2 Most market participants do not expect the HKMA to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar falls to the lower end of the trading band, forcing the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start selling dollars and withdraw Hong Kong dollar liquidity. ($1 = 7.8118 Hong Kong dollars) (Reporting By Rushil Dutta in Bengaluru; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-9-14T09:39:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170914ed9e00b1w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
