\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Hong Kong to offer HK$40 bln in additional Exchange Fund Bills\b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2017\par 08:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * HKMA to add HK$8 bln in 3-months bills in the next five tenders               \par \par \uc2 * Says sees huge demand from banks to manage liquidity               \par \par \uc2 * Says new bills issuance nothing to do with weak HK dollar (Add background, details)               \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Aug 9 (Reuters) - Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it will offer HK$40 billion ($5.11 billion) worth of additional Exchange Fund Bills to meet increased demand by banks, given the abundance of liquidity in the banking system.               \par \par \uc2 The issuance of additional Exchange Fund paper would be conducted by expanding the supply of three-month Exchange Fund Bills, the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) said.               \par \par \uc2 The additional issuance had nothing to do with the trend of the Hong Kong dollar, which this week eased to its weakest level in 18 months.               \par \par \uc2 "The recent weakening of the HKD is not a concern to the HKMA," Hong Kong's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, adding it was natural to see an easing Hong Kong dollar exchange rate due to interest rate discounts between the local and U.S. dollar.               \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been weakening steadily this year, as the interest rates charged by the city's banks have failed to follow U.S. interest rates higher.               \par \par \uc2 The local dollar eased to 7.8277 to the U.S. dollar by midday on Wednesday, its lowest level against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since January 2016.               \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar, but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.               \par \par \uc2 The three-month Exchange Fund Bills will be offered on Aug 22, 29, Sept 5, 12 and 19, and will add an extra HK$8 billion in each of the tender, the HKMA said.               \par \par \uc2 Banks' demand for the bills had been strong in the recent months for liquidity-management purposes, it added.               \par \par \uc2 "Interbank liquidity is expected to remain abundant after the issuance of additional Exchange Fund Bills, which is not expected to have a significant impact on liquidity conditions and interest rates," the HKMA said.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-8-9T07:42:59.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170809ed89007xs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
