\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar to extend weakening trend, driven by excess cash, spreads\b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2017\par 09:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, July 27 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar firmed marginally against its U.S. counterpart on Thursday but traders expect the steady weakening trend since the beginning of the year to continue, driven by excess liquidity and widening interest rate spreads between the territory and the United States.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot rate, which has fallen about 0.7 percent so far this year and is on track for a seventh straight month of decline, was 0.01 percent stronger at 0620 GMT, 86 pips on the weaker side of the peg at 7.8086.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar, but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.\par \par \uc2 Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg arrangement, the city's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the primary reason for the weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a surge in cash flows into Hong Kong because of loose global monetary policy and despite a slowing of capital flows from neighbouring China.\par \par \uc2 "Liquidity has been accumulating in the system since the global financial crisis because of the peg exchange regime. All the liquidity is from loose monetary policy in the United States," said Andy Ji, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Excess liquidity makes the Hong Kong dollar a handy funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for carry trades, whereby investors borrow cheaply in Hong Kong dollars and invest in higher-yielding assets elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 In a June policy meeting, the HKMA raised the base rate charged through its overnight discount window by 25 basis points to 1.50 percent following a rate rise by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Still, spreads between short-term Hong Kong and U.S. rates have been widening in anticipation of faster policy tightening and stimulus withdrawal by the Fed.\par \par \uc2 While the HKMA has been raising the base rate, the HIBOR or the floating rate at which banks lend to each other has been rigid.\par \par \uc2 HIBOR-LIBOR spreads have gradually widened since 2015, and the 3-month spread is now 0.55392 versus -0.02878 basis points at the beginning of 2017. The spread is currently at its widest since September 2008.\par \par \uc2 In the June meeting HKMA chief executive \uc2 Norman Chan\uc2  had warned investors that if the interest rate differential widened further, there would be more arbitrage activities involving fund flows from the Hong Kong dollar to the U.S. dollar, which would spur capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 "The hike of HKD interest rates didn't really push HKD interbank market rate up. The real market interest rate is quite low," said a trader with a mainland bank.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needn't wait for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to breach the lower limit of the trading band to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders believe it will refrain from doing so to allow the economy to strengthen further.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's economy expanded at a robust rate of 4.3 percent in the March quarter from a year earlier, its fastest annual pace in six years.\par \par \uc2 "I think from the perspective of boosting economy, HKMA would like to see a weakened HKD," a trader said.\par \par \uc2 "Also, there's no effective measure to withdraw interbank liquidity by the HKMA, so I think they might want to encourage the weakness of the Hong Kong dollar." (Reporting By Rushil Dutta; Editing by Eric Meijer) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-7-27T08:53:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170727ed7r00ahd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
