\par\par \b \uc2 China's Yuan Surges Offshore, With an Apparent Boost From Beijing\b0\par\par\uc2 By Saumya Vaishampayan \par \uc2 825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2017\par 13:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged to its highest level against the dollar in six months in offshore markets on Wednesday, a move some traders ascribed to \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  meant to warn investors off betting against the yuan following \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgrade of Chinese government debt last week.\par \par \uc2 The yuan rose as high as 6.7677 to the U.S. dollar in the offshore market, centered in Hong Kong, its strongest intraday level since Nov. 4, according to Wind Info. That marked a gain of 0.8% from its level late Tuesday. The yuan also rose in the tightly controlled onshore market, ending 0.6% higher from its Friday close of 6.8210 to the dollar: The onshore market was closed for national holidays on Monday and Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 A sharp rise in the cost for banks to borrow the yuan short-term in Hong Kong was a key driver of its surge, traders and analysts said. The overnight yuan borrowing rate soared to 21.08% on Wednesday from 5.35% on Monday, according to the Hong Kong-based Treasury Markets Association.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the offshore market last week, with some state-owned Chinese banks refraining from lending out yuan in Hong Kong, driving borrowing costs higher. The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  didn't immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Speculation about such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  swirled again on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Alex Wolf, senior emerging markets economist at Standard Life Investments in Hong Kong, was among those who said the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably behind the rise in borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 "There is really no other reason you'd have a spike in yuan-funding costs," he said. "The only way they can really manage the offshore rate is through squeezing liquidity, since it is more market-based."\par \par \uc2 The cost of borrowing the yuan in Hong Kong has surged periodically over the last 18 months, each time helping to push the yuan up against the dollar. Higher short-term borrowing costs make it more expensive for investors to short, or bet on a decline in, the yuan, which often forces them to buy back yuan and sell dollars as they give up on those bets.\par \par \uc2 "We're seeing quite a big positioning washout happening" said Khoon Goh, head of Asia research at ANZ in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 One difference this time is that the yuan has already been appreciating against the dollar, one of many major global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that rose against the greenback in recent weeks. The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on track to gain nearly 2% against the dollar in the offshore market this month.\par \par \uc2 The suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days comes after ratings firm \uc2 Moody's Investors Service\uc2  last week downgraded China's credit rating and warned about the country's high levels of debt.\par \par \uc2 China has shifted to targeting stability in the yuan against the dollar this year, which had already helped curb investors' expectations for how much the yuan might fall in the coming months. The likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent days suggests China still felt the need to deter investors overseas from viewing the \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgrade as a reason to turn bearish.\par \par \uc2 "It is a bit of an overreaction, but I wouldn't necessarily put it past them," Mr. Wolf said, referring to Chinese authorities.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently been guiding the yuan to stronger-than-expected levels in the onshore market, another sign that it is seeking to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has also tweaked the way it calculates its daily fix for the yuan-dollar pair, adding a "countercyclical" component that lets it exert more control over the yuan's value.\par \par \uc2 Investors appear to be responding to the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In a shift, those using options are now bracing for further gains in the offshore yuan over the next month.\par \par \uc2 The one-month risk reversal for the dollar against the yuan turned negative on Friday, which means bearish put options on the dollar against the offshore yuan are now more expensive than bullish call options. Investors would typically buy bearish put options on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair if they expect the dollar to fall against the yuan over a specific period. An options contract grants the right to buy or sell the underlying asset.\par \par \uc2 That risk reversal is now at its most negative level ever, according to \uc2 Thomson Reuters\uc2  data going back to 2013. However, longer-dated risk reversals remain positive, suggesting investors are still bracing for yuan depreciation over the next few months.\par \par \uc2 "The bias is now shifting to one which is favoring short-term [yuan] appreciation," said Eddie Cheung, Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Standard Chartered Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Saumya Vaishampayan at saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 31, 2017 07:30 ET (11:30 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170531ed5v001a1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
