\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Hong Kong overnight yuan lending rate eases after 7-mth high fixing\b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2016\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * CNH overnight borrowing rate fixed at 5.5155 pct\par \par \uc2 * That rate hits 10 pct, then eases to about 2 pct\par \par \uc2 * Volatile CNH Hibor partly due to \uc2 PBOC\uc2  actions - traders (Adds comments, details)\par \par \uc2 By Michelle Chen\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Sept 12 (Reuters) - Hong Kong's overnight yuan borrowing rate eased to around 2 percent after hitting 10 percent on Monday morning amid volatile trading following its fixing at a seven-month high.\par \par \uc2 The CNH Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate benchmark (CNH Hibor), set by the city's Treasury Markets Association (TMA), was fixed at 5.5155 percent for overnight contracts, the highest level since Feb. 19. Friday's fixing was 4.71267 percent.\par \par \uc2 Offshore yuan borrowing rates have been elevated since late last week, and market players have different theories on why. Some say \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the borrowing rates higher to dampen yuan short-sellers, and others believe it is just due to short-term liquidity concerns.\par \par \uc2 "The surging CNH Hibor is just a natural result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year," a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  "has brought yuan funds back to onshore market after their forward positions here matured," said the trader, adding that he did not see any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the CNH market recently.\par \par \uc2 "The offshore yuan market actually does not lack liquidity, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action has a big psychological impact on it," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 RESIDUAL FROM 2015\par \par \uc2 Sue Trinh, head of Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Royal Bank of Canada\uc2  in Hong Kong, agreed.\par \par \uc2 "It's pretty much the residual left over from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that we saw last year that was unsterilized," Trinh said, noting that liquidity was tight now just for short-term contracts such as overnight ones.\par \par \uc2 In August 2015, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  orchestrated a significant depreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , followed by a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  both onshore and offshore to stabilise market expectations.\par \par \uc2 The overnight yuan borrowing rate fell to around 2 percent at 0835GMT Monday.\par \par \uc2 However, traders say the CNH Hibor may remain volatile in the coming days as market players need time to digest the actions from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reallocate their yuan funds.\par \par \uc2 "The offshore yuan market is definitely not in panic or lack liquidity like what happened last year or at the beginning of this year," said a senior banker at a Chinese bank in Hong Kong, adding that a range of rumours impacted the market. (Additional reporting by John Ruwith in Shanghai; Editing by Richard Borsuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-9-12T10:27:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160912ec9c00gqw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
