\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA MARKETS: Nikkei Surges Nearly 6%, Leading Asian Market Rebound\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chao Deng   \par \uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2016\par 09:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Japan stocks jump as energy shares recover\par \par \uc2 Japan's Nikkei Stock Average soared Friday amid a broad Asia market rally that capped off a volatile week, as investors put their hopes in more stimulus from major central banks.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei 225 index closed nearly 5.9% up, at 16,958.5 -- the largest daily percentage gain since Sept. 9.\par \par \uc2 Traders said investors were taking off bets that the Japanese yen will strengthen for the time being, weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and boosting stocks. The Japanese yen has weakened to Yen118.03 to one U.S. dollar, from as strong as Yen116.45 late Thursday afternoon in Asia. That is about a 1.4% decline.\par \par \uc2 Traders attributed the positive sentiment to building expectations that the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will still ease policy, as well as comments from Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 's aide on Thursday in Asia that "conditions for additional easing have fallen into place." The aide's comments coincide with speculation that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might increase its asset-purchasing program at its Jan. 28-29 meeting. Since Autumn 2014, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying Yen80 trillion ($685 billion) annually in assets.\par \par \uc2 "The comments from Abe's [aide] suggest everything's being considered," said Andrew Sullivan, managing director at Haitong International. Given that investors had such bearish positions at the beginning of the year, they are switching their trades in case the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  eases next week, he said.\par \par \uc2 The Shanghai Composite Index closed nearly up 1.3% after a choppy morning of trading, as investors assessed comments by officials on the domestic market at the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  in Davos, Switzerland.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index was last up 3% and Australia's S&P/ASX 200 ended up 1%. South Korea's Kospi gained 2.1%.\par \par \uc2 The gains marked a break from recent selling that pushed Japan's stock market into bear-market territory earlier in the week, joining Hong Kong and China. A bear market is a drop of at least 20% from a recent high.\par \par \uc2 Energy shares in the region rose as Brent oil prices broke the $30 mark per barrel, up 4.8% to $30.65. Worries about weaker global growth had been reflected in new lows for oil prices earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 In Europe Thursday, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  said the bank may need to review its policy stance at its next meeting, indicating the bank could be open to more stimulus measures. U.S. stocks pushed higher, with the Dow Jones Industrial Average climbing 0.7%. The Stoxx Europe 600 advanced 1.9%.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday in Davos, Switzerland, China's Vice President \uc2 Li Yuanchao\uc2  signaled that Beijing would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its stock market in an interview that was widely circulated by local media.\par \par \uc2 The Shanghai Composite Index had plunged 3.2% on Thursday, as widening losses in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  and signs of lessening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Beijing spooked investors. The benchmark is down 18% year-to-date.\par \par \uc2 In Japan, shares of \uc2 Sharp Corp\uc2 . (6753.TO) finished up 3%, after a report by the local media outlet the Nikkei that a Japanese government-backed fund will take a majority stake in the electronics maker and is asking the two creditor banks to hand over Yen200 billion ($1.70 billion) in Sharp's preferred shares. Foxconn, formally known as \uc2 Hon Hai Precision Industry\uc2 , has also offered about Yen625 billion to take over Sharp.\par \par \uc2 Gold prices edged up 0.1% at $1,099.40 a troy ounce.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 22, 2016 03:40 ET (08:40 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160122ec1m0017p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
