\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong Stocks on Shaky Ground as Weak China Data Sinks In -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2016\par 02:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0111 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Hong Kong stocks are headed for a lackluster session Wednesday weighed by concerns over the slowing China economy and depressed crude-oil prices. Investors were hoping for fresh stimulus from the Chinese government, which buoyed market sentiment Tuesday. Some of it is coming: \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday that it would inject 600 billion yuan ($91 billion) into the financial system to provide liquidity before the Chinese Lunar New Year holiday. But their' mood is darkening as they digest the bad news highlighted in China data, which "was that economic momentum slowed in December," says ING. Hang Seng Index futures were down 1% before the market open. The Hong Kong dollar also weakened overnight to 7.8178 per U.S. dollar, flirting with the threshold that would prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  and raising questions about how much money is leaving the city. (dominique.fong@wsj.com; @dominiquefong) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0106 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The construction of the Thailand-China rail links with a total distance of some 963 kilometers (598 miles) will continue to be discussed by a joint committee in Beijing in February after China has assured the interest rate for the financing of the project will be 2.0%, according to Thai Transport Minister Arkhom Termpittayapaisith. Among issues to be raised include the adjustment of the investment ratio between Thailand and China to 30:70 from 40:60 and the expanded area of coverage by China's investment, the minister says. "The adjustment of China's [investment] proportion is intended to have China take more risks," adds Arkhom, who notes that the start of the actual construction will still be in May of this year.(nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@wsj.com; @nopbkk) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0058 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japanese stocks are down as concerns smolder about any economic disruptions from sharply lower crude oil prices and continued uncertainty over the U.S. monetary policy outlook. Mining and oil-related stocks are leading declines. Oil explorer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inpex Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (1605.TO) is down 2.5% at Y972.1. Oil distributor \f28 \uc2 \f2 JX Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (5020.TO) is down 2.4% at Y423.6. U.S. oil prices declined again on Tuesday, falling to new 12-year lows. Nikkei is down 0.8% at 16915.68. (kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0052 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] A Tuesday warning from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  that oil prices could slide further south, due to oversupply, dampened a nascent return of risk appetite. Wall Street's failed attempt to rally overnight, combined with the retreat of the risk-sensitive commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --after staging a brief intraday rally--suggest that risk aversion is back on the cards Wednesday. The disappointing China economic data released Tuesday may hence come back to haunt jittery investors, even if stocks on the benchmark Shanghai composite index ended 3.2% higher yesterday. Shanghai's rally was surprising, given the less-than-stellar gross domestic product data released. China's fourth-quarter growth of 6.8% fell short of analysts' expectations for a rise of 6.9%, while full-year GDP growth was 6.9%--the slowest pace in 25 years. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0042 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The return of risk aversion, once again due to the deteriorating outlook for crude oil prices - which hint at weak global economic growth ahead - could restart a technical rally for USD/SGD. The greenback temporarily lost its bullish bias against the Singapore dollar Tuesday, when it closed below the floor of the Bollinger uptrend channel. But USD/SGD is now clawing its way back up, and could end Wednesday above 1.4393 - which would then reinstate the Bollinger uptrend channel. That could get USD/SGD back on course toward the round-figure trading barrier of 1.4500, and possibly to the ceiling of the uptrend channel, currently at 1.4520. On Tuesday, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  warned that the oil glut could worsen, which spooked U.S. stocks, sent commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower, and sparked a retreat of oil prices back toward its 2003-lows. USD/SGD is now 1.4375 from its Tuesday close of 1.4368. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0036 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/MYR is rising Wednesday, and could reinstate the Bollinger uptrend channel - which would hint at further ringgit weakness versus the dollar ahead - after crude oil prices subsided overnight. Brent crude oil retreated toward its 2003-low and now lingers below $29 per barrel, after a warning from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  that the oil glut could worsen. The key factor that has the oil market worried is the return of Iran's oil exports into the global inventory, following the lifting of sanctions. U.S. stocks gave up an initial rally, and the Australia dollar surrendered some of its intraday gains Tuesday - hinting that risk aversion may be returning. If USD/MYR rallies higher and closes above the 4.3920 entrance of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, it would be a negative cue for the Malaysia ringgit. USD/MYR is now 4.3800 from its Tuesday close of 4.3630. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0033 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/KRW opened higher Wednesday, reflecting a deterioration of risk appetite that was primarily due to oil prices retreating overnight, after a warning from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  that the oil glut could worsen. The change in market sentiment was evident in the turnaround of U.S. stocks from strength to end nearly unchanged, as well as in the pullback of the Australian dollar - a key commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that acts as a gauge of global investor confidence. USD/KRW is inching back up due to a tentative return of risk aversion, and may soon reinstate the Bollinger uptrend channel. A Wednesday closing above 1,208 would confirm the bullish-USD technical cue, which would suggest that the South Korea won will continue to weaken versus the greenback in the near term. USD/KRW is now 1,209.3 from its Tuesday close of 1,205.9. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0025 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The New Zealand dollar has fallen sharply after a weaker-than-expected inflation reading Wednesday. New Zealand's consumer price index fell 0.5% in the December quarter, pulling annual inflation down to 0.1%, which is its lowest reading since September 1999. The NZD/USD fell below US$0.6400 after the data release from around US$0.6475 prior, and is currently trading at US$0.6408. Some economists expect the RBNZ to cut rates by up to 50 basis points this year to try to pull inflation back within its 1% to 3% target range. (kate.geenty@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2306 GMT -- The USD/JPY "will likely remain directionless," placing the pair (now at 117.62) to trade in a 117.20-118.20 range during Asia trade, says Toshiyuki Umekawa, senior vice president of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  division at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "We saw a big fall in oil prices overnight, but that's unlikely to help intensify risk aversion mood," due to stability in China yuan and stocks, says Umekawa. (Light, sweet crude down 3.3% to $28.46 a barrel in New York on worries that the lifting of sanctions on Iran could increase oil supply.) Ahead of \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  policy meeting Thursday, investors may take a wait-and-see stance, positioning the EUR/USD (now at 1.0907) to move in a 1.0850-1.1950 range. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2140 GMT - The Australian dollar firmed overnight on improving risk sentiment, said CBA strategist Elias Haddad. European equities rallied and most commodity prices are higher. The improvement in risk sentiment during the European session may stem from participants extrapolating that Chinese policymakers could soon act to support growth, he said. Still, CBA continues to expect the Aussie dollar to edge lower over the months ahead because of global growth concerns, shaky financial market conditions, and the lower Australian terms of trade. Consumer confidence data at 2330 GMT might induce some intraday volatility, he adds. The Australian dollar currently trades at US$0.6915. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2135 GMT - Expect to see plenty of positive news flow from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dacian Gold\f28 \uc2 \f2  (DCN.AU), says Canaccord Genuity. The junior miner has outlined a major drilling program and recently appointed GR Engineering to advance feasibility works on its Mt Morgans gold project in Western Australia state. That should help to put \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dacian Gold\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a position to make a final decision on whether to develop the gold mine at Mt Morgans by the end of the year, boosting its appeal as a takeover candidate. "We maintain our speculative buy recommendation and A$1.25/share price target on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dacian Gold\f28 \uc2 \f2 , emphasising the potential scale and cost profile of its Mt Morgans project as highly attractive relative to its producing peer group," Canaccord says. DCN last traded at A$0.80. (david.winning@wsj.com; @dwinningWSJ)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2126 GMT - Canaccord Genuity urges investors to keep the faith with Sino Gas and Energy Holdings (SEH.AU), after a series of missed milestones significantly jolted market confidence in the realization of the company's value. Topping the list of negative news specific to the company was the receipt of payment for gas sales for the past year. "While our valuation has changed only slightly, down just A$0.02/share to A$0.29/share, and we retain our buy rating, we expect market confidence (and Sino Gas and Energy's ability to trend towards valuation) is likely to remain low until an improved track record of milestone delivery can be achieved over several months," Canaccord says. SEH last traded at 2.9 Australian cents. (david.winning@wsj.com; @dwinningWSJ)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 19, 2016 20:11 ET (01:11 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160120ec1k0006x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
