\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Stocks Rebound on China GDP, Oil Recovery -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2016\par 10:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0927 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] An unexpected leap higher in crude oil prices helps propel a recovery, Tuesday, for Singapore's FTSE Straits Times Index, which ends the day up 1.8% at 2638.47. Markets were also likely buoyed by Chinese GDP data for 2015, which came in within expectations. Oil-linked companies surged, led by rig builders \uc2 SembCorp Marine\uc2  (S51.SG) and \uc2 Keppel Corp\uc2  (BN4.SG), up 12.6% and 6.8%, respectively. Commodity firm \uc2 Noble Group\uc2  (N21.SG) ends 9.1% higher. Among other movers is Hyflux (600.SG), up 6.3% on a contract win, while \uc2 Keppel REIT\uc2  (K71U.SG) rises 2.3% on the back of its quarterly results. The day is not without losers, however. Telcos StarHub (CC3.SG) and \uc2 Singapore Telecommunications\uc2  (Z74.SG) fall 2.1% and 0.9%, respectively, after their smaller competitor M1 (B2F.SG) reported weak quarterly results. M1 ends 4.2% lower. (jake.watts@wsj.com; Twitter: @jmwatts_) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0923 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Jakarta Composite Index ends 0.2% higher at 4491.74, Tuesday, rising slightly in line with most other Asian markets after oil prices rose and China reported full-year GDP numbers that were within expectations, lifting a risk concern for Asian markets. Most large-caps gain, if only a little. Telco \uc2 XL Axiata\uc2  (EXCL.JK) ends up 3.3% and Indofood Sukses Makmur (INDF.JK) rises 2.6%. Losers include \uc2 Perusahaan Gas Negara\uc2  (PGAS.JK) and Gudang Garam (GGRM.JK), down 1.8% and 0.9%, respectively. Despite the overall gains in Indonesian markets, investors are hit with warnings from rating agencies during the session. Fitch warns of a speculative selloff in the rupiah after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates last week. \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  says Indonesian corporates' credit trend will likely stay negative. (jake.watts@wsj.com; Twitter: @jmwatts_) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0903 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China SCE Property (1966.HK) will mainly seek financing in China's onshore market, such as project loans or bonds, financial controller Paul Li told The Wall Street Journal, citing cheaper rates at home and the yuan's fall as drivers. SCE Property in October 2015 issued 2 billion yuan five-year onshore bonds with a 5.18% coupon and issued a further 1.5 billion yuan onshore bonds with 5.30% coupon in December 2015. Earlier this month, it has announced plans to redeem all its outstanding US$350 million, 11.50% U.S. dollar bonds due 2017, funded by US$400 million syndicate loan it signed on January 4. Li said the company's average funding cost is expected to fall to below 7.5% in 2016 from 9.5% at end-2014 after recent financing practices and consecutive rate cuts in China. As the company expands its borrowings in China's onshore market, the company's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  debt to its total debt proportion, has been reduced to around one-third of its total debt, versus around 40% as at end-2014, he adds. (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0858 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Hong Kong dollar continues to weaken Tuesday, edging up to the level that would force the city's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar is trading at 7.81 per U.S. dollar, and if the exchange rate hits 7.85, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will step in to defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . As the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  skirts closer to the threshold, more money may be flowing out of Hong Kong. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  says Hong Kong's liquidity-rich banking system could afford to lose up to HK$300 billion. To prevent huge outflows, Hong Kong must raise interest rates to draw money back to the city, says Raymond Ngai, head of Hong Kong and China property research for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 ." If the Hong Kong interbank rate [Hibor] were to go up to the same as the Libor rate," meaning that local rates would match the more attractive U.S. rates, "the pace of capital outflow would probably come down," he says. (dominique.fong@wsj.com; Twitter: @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0852 GMT The squeezed U.K. inflation-linked market is up for a bounce if Tuesday's inflation data beats expectations, as especially the front end prices a subdued outlook, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 . This is the last price index release before February's Inflation Report and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects a retail price index print of +1.2% year-on-year, which is 20 bps above with the WSJ poll. RPI indexation is the convention for U.K. linkers. The bank also sees a consumer price index print of +0.2% year-on-year, 10 bps higher than the WSJ poll. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0850 GMT Austrian consumer prices harmonized according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  standards rose 1.1% on the year in December compared with a 0.5% increase in November, the country's statistics office says Tuesday. The indicator, calculated according to national standards, was up 1.0% on the year after 0.6% in the previous month. The statistics office says the main reason behind the increase was the price development of crude oil, which was 12.1% cheaper in December, while in November it was down 15.3% on annual comparison. (emese.bartha@wjs.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0848 GMT Eurozone government bonds are trading slightly weaker Tuesday as risk-on seems to have made a comeback in equities and energy today. Worse-than-expected growth data in China triggered a bounce for equities - another example of "bad news is good news", says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  rate strategist Richard McGuire, as it points to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stimulus. Germany is outperforming its U.K. and U.S. counterparts, rising 1 bp in yield versus 6 bps and 3.5 bps respectively. However, the low growth/low inflation backdrop is set to remain, providing support for bonds, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0829 GMT Deflationary pressures intensified in Switzerland last month with a steep drop in producer and import prices. The combined index fell 5.5% on the year, a larger fall than expected by economists. The producer price component fell 3.6% annually while import prices slid 9.7% from December 2014. All in all, this keeps pressure on the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to maintain an ultra-loose monetary policy. (brian.blackstone@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0828 GMT A rebound in risk appetite in China on one hand and a possible negative surprise in the ZEW survey on the other don't give a clear direction to the Bund futures contract Tuesday, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It sees limited room for further gains today, as markets will speculate on the next \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actions amid deteriorating inflation expectations. The Eurex-listed continuous contract is trading at around 160.20 in early Tuesday morning, slightly lower than the previous close. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0828 GMT Economic sentiment in Germany is expected to weaken in January, according to The Wall Street Journal's survey. The ZEW indicator of economic expectations, due at 1000 GMT, is seen having fallen to 8.0 in January from 16.1 in December. "Given the nature of this survey, we expect a more pessimistic reading, reflecting developments in financial markets since turn of the year," say analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0827 GMT A lower jet fuel bill due to weak oil prices and an ambitious restructuring plan is good news for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Air France-KLM\f28 \uc2 \f2 's credit, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which raises its recommendation on the June 2021 bond issue to buy from hold. It also switches to buy from hold on a 6.25% hybrid with a first call in October 2020. SocGen recommends selling protection via five-year credit default swaps while buying five-year CDS of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lufthansa\f28 \uc2 \f2  to benefit from convergence. The average Brent price should stand at $42.5 in 2016, which is less than the $55 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Air France\f28 \uc2 \f2  assumed to calculate its $5.7 billion post-hedging jet fuel bill. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0825 GMT Fundamental changes in policy implemented by Portugal's new left-wing government could lead to a further rise in public debt and to the erosion of the country's competitiveness, say \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts. While it's questionable how long the government will continue with this course, a further marked deterioration of the budget situation carries the risk that DBRS, the last ratings agency to peg Portugal's credit rating in investment-grade territory, will also move it to junk when it reviews the country at the end of April, it says. That would mean \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  wouldn't be able to buy any Portuguese bonds without a new rescue program, they say. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 19, 2016 04:27 ET (09:27 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160119ec1j001fk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
