\par\par \b \uc2 Bets Against Yuan Face Rocky Road\b0\par\par\uc2 By Mia Lamar and Anjani Trivedi   \par \uc2 902 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2016\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--In mid-November at the Grand Hyatt hotel in midtown Manhattan, prominent hedge-fund investor \uc2 David Tepper\uc2  told an audience gathered to hear money-making ideas that "the problem with China right now is they have a very overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gyrations so far this year have in part borne out forecasts made by the likes of Mr. Tepper, whose \uc2 Appaloosa Management LP\uc2  is one of Wall Street's most successful firms. They have also underscored one big risk faced by those betting against the yuan--the chance the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall.\par \par \uc2 Now, following the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's successful fight back against what it has called "speculators" driving down the yuan's value, the question is whether the markets will continue to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve.\par \par \uc2 Investors from New York to Hong Kong stepped up bets against the yuan late last year in the so-called offshore market for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , convinced it was set for another fall against the dollar following the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 's decision on Nov. 30 to add the yuan to its elite basket of reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The offshore yuan slid as much as 2.7% in the first four trading days of the year, a major move by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market standards. But from Friday onwards, heavy yuan buying by Chinese state-owned banks--prompted by the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 --saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bounce back as much as 2.9% from its weakest level last week.\par \par \uc2 "It's a risky trade," said Allen Sing, a portfolio manager at SAIL Advisors Ltd. in Hong Kong, which invests in hedge funds. "It's a bet against policy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which doesn't make sense in this environment."\par \par \uc2 After 2016's rocky start, investors and traders say they now expect a period of calm and are reluctant to place new bets just yet. Sentiment toward the yuan, though, remains fragile.\par \par \uc2 Many said they expect the yuan to gradually weaken as the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  grapples with giving market forces a bigger role to allow the yuan to decline against the U.S. dollar, with its familiar urge to maintain a tight grip on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fight speculators.\par \par \uc2 "Certainly the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has discovered a new way of managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is through liquidity," said one hedge-fund manager that has been betting against the yuan. "The difficult part is what's next. I think we stay in a pretty stable zone."\par \par \uc2 Investors bearish on the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year expected the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's decision would encourage Beijing to show its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime had become more liberal, reducing the risk of any sudden government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if, as they expected, the yuan headed downwards.\par \par \uc2 "There was a sentiment that 'OK, we can take our chances now,'" said SAIL Advisors' Mr. Sing. "There was a sense of extreme bearishness, especially the further away you got from Asia."\par \par \uc2 Yet traders say anxiety was still running high that Beijing would eventually step in. Some investors darted in and out of the trade, putting on bearish positions for just hours at a time, according to traders. One hedge-fund manager betting against the yuan said he cut a two-week old position by about 75% over the past week, satisfied with the profit he had made.\par \par \uc2 The warning sign for many was the increased divergence between the yuan's value in offshore markets, where it was falling fast, and its price in the less open domestic Chinese market, where it was dropping less quickly. Traders sensed the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  wouldn't allow the gap to widen too far for fear it would only encourage offshore investors to increase their negative bets.\par \par \uc2 That hunch proved correct as Chinese banks started buying up the yuan in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week, a sign the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say. Their buying pushed the cost of borrowing yuan up sharply, making it more expensive to carry out trades betting against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some nimble investors have been rewarded. Carl Huttenlocher, who runs the $4 billion Hong Kong hedge fund Myriad Asset Management, scored on bearish bets against the yuan, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 One of Asia's best-known traders, Mr. Huttenlocher had been building the position over the past year, one of the people said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Huttenlocher and other investors used bearish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -options and forwards to build up positions that the yuan would weaken, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Mr. Tepper declined to comment on his bets against the yuan.\par \par \uc2 Many, like \uc2 Adam Levinson\uc2 , a former star trader at Fortress Investment Group LLC executive who runs Singapore-based hedge fund Graticule Asset Management Asia, expect further declines for the yuan.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to investors dated Jan. 12, Mr. Levinson said his fund had made money betting on a weaker yuan with profitable options trades as recently as last month.\par \par \uc2 "We maintain our view that the yuan will continue to depreciate over the medium-term," Mr. Levinson wrote in the letter, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded onshore. He didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Write to Mia Lamar at mia.lamar@wsj.com and Anjani Trivedi at anjani.trivedi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 14-01-16 0300GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160114ec1e00032\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
