\par\par \b \uc2 Traders Could Search for Gains in Oversold HK Stocks -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2016\par 02:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0123 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  stocks Tuesday will be heavily influenced by how China \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and battered stock markets. Traders are looking for any chance to buy oversold equities, including signals from China to implement more market-supporting policies. Hang Seng Index futures are up 0.5%. "If we see heavy state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the mainland equity markets alongside these new moves to prop up the CNY, then this could be the jump start needed to see a bit of buying come back into global equities" at least in the short term, brokerage IG says in a note. Expectations of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were driven by an overnight statement from Ma Jun, the chief economist at the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 . He said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to create a new system to "appropriately limit" daily yuan-versus-U.S. dollar volatility. (dominique.fong@wsj.com; @dominiquefong) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0117 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Shares of Sharp (6753.TO) are up 1.8% to 116 yen following reports of a possible bailout by a government-led fund and Sharp's main lenders. The Nikkei reported that, under a proposal made by the government-led Innovation Network of Japan, Sharp would receive an investment of some 200 billion yen ($1.68 billion). Also, 150 billion yen of the loans from the two main lenders would be transferred to a new liquid crystal display entity and converted to preferred shares. (kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0112 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The search for growth in the Australian economy is set to remain a nagging problem for policymakers in 2016, says Pimco. The dominant question going forward will continue to be what will fill the hole left by the mining sector? That question is set to get even more urgent as stimulus to the economy from a housing construction booms fades, Pimco adds in a research note. "This is not to say we envision a significant housing correction, but we certainly expect the housing market tailwind to subside," it said. The less than spectacular growth environment in Australian will leave open the question of whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will need to cut interest rates further from their current record low of 2.0%. (james.glynn@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1106 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] After being triggered twice on two trading days, China's circuit breaker rules were scrapped by regulators the same week they were introduced. The rules halted trading for 15 minutes if the CSI 300 fell by 5% and for the full day if the index dropped by 7%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says China's circuit-breaker rules--versions of which are commonly seen in other markets around the world--failed for three reasons. First, they shut down liquidity. Second, the circuit breaker prevented brokerages from selling shares pledged against loans, should a client fail to meet a margin call. Finally, the circuit breaker led to collapsed brokerage commissions--on Jan. 7, China share turnover shrank to 188 billion yuan ($28.6 billion) (compared with a daily average of 1.05 trillion yuan for 2015)--because trading was halted. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  didn't say, but might have added, that the rules were designed to curtail volatility but had done anything but. (jasper.moiseiwitsch@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @moiseiwitsch) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KBC \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0050 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely keep its policy rate on hold at the current record-low 1.5% for a seventh consecutive month when its policy board meets later this week. The latest Wall Street Journal poll shows 19 of 20 analysts surveyed expect \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  to stand pat on the benchmark seven-day repurchase rate at its Jan. 14 meeting. Only one analyst expects a quarter-percentage-point rate cut at the upcoming meeting. The BOK may want to "take more time to assess the growing drag from China's weakening appetite for its [Korea's] exports" before probably easing further in February or March to help spur anemic growth, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  says in a note. Recent BOK minutes hint that the bank may trim its growth forecast of 3.2% for 2016 in a new outlook on Jan. 14. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0042 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The daily EUR/USD chart is currently inconclusive, while the pair remains stuck inside the Ichimoku Cloud consolidation zone that spans 1.0790-1.1017, and also within a no-man's land demarcated by the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1). Unless EUR/USD manages to end Tuesday out of the 1.0828-1.0951 range suggested by the Bollinger bands, in so doing triggering the Bollinger downtrend or uptrend channels, technical consolidation is likely to persist. The overnight rise of U.S. stocks, and the possibility of a further recovery of China's yuan - based on Monday's sharp gain for the offshore yuan, which is a factor in determining the daily USD/CNY benchmark rate onshore - could help general risk-taking appetite to improve, which would be bearish for the EUR/USD pair because the euro behaves like a funding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . EUR/USD is now 1.0861 from its Monday close of 1.0859. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0034 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/SGD slipped Monday from its 2009 peak of 1.4442 to close lower, after the strengthening of China's yuan sparked a similar reaction across Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But the USD/SGD pair bounced ahead of the 1.4302 base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel - a bullish chart pattern which has been kept intact - suggesting that a rebound higher might take place soon. Whether or not this chart floor holds Tuesday really depends on whether the yuan will add to Monday's 0.4% recovery. Based on movements in the offshore yuan, which is a factor in determining the daily USD/CNY benchmark rate onshore, there is a high chance that \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will adjust the daily yuan benchmark stronger against the U.S. dollar, which would have a bearish effect on USD/SGD. USD/SGD is now 1.4355 from its Monday close of 1.4340. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0030 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] While other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are enjoying a brief respite, on expectations that China's yuan could regain some more of its losses, the ringgit remains weak versus the greenback, trading at 4.3900 from its Monday close of 4.3800. The ringgit is unlikely to rally much while crude oil prices plumb to new lows. The price of Brent crude oil now lingers near its weakest level since April 2004, as the possibility of a stronger U.S. dollar compounds the already-negative supply and demand effects that have recently crushed oil prices. Based on movements in the offshore yuan, which is a factor in determining the daily USD/CNY benchmark rate onshore, there is a high chance that \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will adjust the daily yuan benchmark stronger against the U.S. dollar, which would have a bearish effect on most USD/Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pairs. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0017 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] South Korea's won is clawing back some of the losses notched Monday, which saw it fall to its weakest against the U.S. dollar since 2010. USD/KRW is now lower at 1,206.4 from its last close of 1,209.8, representing a 0.3% strengthening of the won versus the greenback. The rebound of stocks on Wall Street overnight may be helping to soften demand for the safe haven U.S. dollar, but the other reason most USD/Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pairs are slipping is that China's yuan recovered Monday, rising 0.4% against the dollar. If the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again guides the yuan toward strength, other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will follow. While the won is in the midst of rebuilding, the benchmark Kospi stock index is up 0.6%, recovering from its 1.2% drop on Monday. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0012 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Outstanding Japanese bank loans rise 2.2% from a year earlier in December, the weakest growth in 20 months, according to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The latest figure compares with a 2.3% increase in November, marking the fourth straight slowdown for the monthly data. The December result offer a fresh indication that the economy is barely gaining momentum despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's aggressive easing policy that is keeping borrowing costs at very low levels for firms and households. That Japanese companies now hold a record amount of cash and deposits--a reflection of their reluctance to invest or raise wages aggressively in the face of Japan's uncertain growth prospects--may also explain why demand for bank loans isn't strengthening. (takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Futures markets suggested the S&P/ASX200 would open 13 points higher. "Australia Shares Set to Open Lower, as Commodities Fall -- Market Talk," at 22:43 GMT, misstated in the headline and the item that Australia shares were set to open lower.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2257 GMT - The resignation of \f28 \uc2 \f2 3P Learning\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (3PL.AU) CEO \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tim Power\f28 \uc2 \f2  has increased the chances of the online education provider becoming a takeover target, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. "This view reflects \f28 \uc2 \f2 3P Learning\f28 \uc2 \f2 's significant share price weakness in the past 3 months, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness in the past year, relatively entrenched customer base and \f28 \uc2 \f2 3P Learning\f28 \uc2 \f2 's established position in the Australian and UK markets and a growing presence in the Americas," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. Still, the broker cuts its price target by 20% to A$1.92/share, as Power's resignation is a clear short-term negative for the company. 3PL last traded at A$1.63. (david.winning@wsj.com; @dwinningWSJ)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 11, 2016 20:23 ET (01:23 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160112ec1c00044\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
