\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Shares Open Lower on Chinese Jitters -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,705 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2016\par 05:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0434 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India shares have opened lower on worries over China. Though analysts have repeatedly said India is more resilient to external shocks, either from China or elsewhere, investor sentiment is badly hit, market operators say. The S&P \uc2 BSE\uc2  Sensex is down 1.2% at 24,640.10, a 52-week low, while the CNX Nifty is down 1.1% at 7,514.40. Metal stocks, that are closely linked to China, are down, namely \uc2 Tata Steel\uc2  (500470.BY) which is down 3% and the biggest Sensex loser, followed by \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2  (500112.BY) down 2.4% and \uc2 Bharat Heavy Electricals\uc2  (500103.BY) down 2.3%. \uc2 Infosys (500209.BY) \uc2 is least declining stock on the Sensex down 0.1% followed by \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) down 0.3% and \uc2 Hero MotoCorp\uc2  (500182.BY) down 0.7%. (kenan.machado@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0402 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] A countercyclical buffer recently introduced by \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  provides it with a tool to persuade banks to conserve capital and slow credit growth that could help the country during its current slowing cycle, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  said Monday. "To the extent that the increase in the capital buffer prompts banks to conserve capital and slow their balance sheet growth, it would benefit their credit quality," the report said. The rule took effect at the start of the month as part of efforts to fully adopt the Basel III regulations that determine banks capital adequacy norms. The countercyclical buffer requirement was initially set at 0% of banks' risk-weighted assets, which \uc2 Moody's\uc2  said was likely due to a decline in credit growth in Indonesia and a subdued outlook for economic growth. (sara.schonhardt@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0357 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Vietnam is seeking to boost its stock market, including by attracting more foreign investment, Finance Minister Dinh Tien Dung said. Dung said his ministry is working on ways to boost the implementation of a government decree to remove the limit on foreign ownership of locally listed companies. He said Vietnam will also seek to improve the local stock market's credit rating and cut down on administrative procedures to facilitate the participation of foreign investors in the market. Dung said that Vietnam's stock market grew 6.1% last year, with the total market capitalization equaling 57% of the GDP at the end of 2015. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter: @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0353 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The liquidity in the offshore yuan market is drying up, squeezing short-term interbank borrowing rates to extreme levels. On Monday morning, the overnight rate that banks in Hong Kong charge each other to borrow yuan soared from 4% Friday to 13.4% (annualized), an all-time high since the Treasury Markets Association started publishing this benchmark rate in 2013. The one-week (annualized) rate surged to 11.23% from 7.05% Friday. It comes after Chinese banks, proxy for \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market and bought up the yuan last week. "As these banks are holding the yuan instead of releasing it to the market, liquidity has dried up," says a senior trader at a major local bank. "A lot of channels bringing money from onshore to offshore market have been blocked, which also contributes to the shortage of yuan in Hong Kong," said Tommy Ong, head of Wealth Management Solutions at DBS in Hong Kong. This effectively increased the cost for speculators to borrow and short the yuan, traders say. The spot CNH, or offshore yuan, has become quieter in transaction and stabilized in value. The USD/CNH stands up 6.6727 versus 6.6820 late Friday. (fiona.law@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0333 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Lower crude oil prices will allow Vietnam to continue to cut its input costs to make Vietnamese exports more competitive, boosting economic growth, Minister of Finance Dinh Tien Dung said. Dung said faster economic growth will create more budget revenue, compensating for a decline in revenue from crude oil exports. He said Vietnam is prepared for the scenario where crude oil prices stay as low as $30 per barrel for this year. He said Vietnam will pursue a market-based price for transport fuels. Last year, Vietnam cut transport fuel prices by 12%-30% for different types of products. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter: @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "China's economy is beset with a host of problems, but inflation isn't one. Consumer price inflation remains high enough to keep concerns about deflation at bay but low enough to give policymakers plenty of room to loosen further," says Williams. "China Has Problems, but Inflation Isn't One of Them -- Market Talk," at 0219 GMT, misquoted Capital Economics economist Mark Williams.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0322 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Australia's unemployment rate might have further to fall based on current indicators of hiring and job creation, says ANZ chief economist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Warren Hogan\f28 \uc2 \f2 . He made the comment while pointing to a solid 0.8% trend growth in job advertising in December from November. "The positive job ads trend suggests that the jobless rate should remain below 6% in coming months and could even improve a little further, he added. Official data has shown 130,000 new jobs added over the last two months, with unemployment at an 18 month low of 5.8%. If ANZ is right, ongoing signs of improvement in the job market will go a long way to keeping the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  sidelined. It has remained chilled out since May, keeping the cash rate at 2.0%. It also notes the Australian dollar is knocking on the door of its lowest levels since October 2009. The hurdle to cut rates further might be more than just another soft quarterly inflation read. Fourth quarter CPI data is due January 27. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter: @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0319 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mogujie.com\f28 \uc2 \f2 , one of China's biggest fashion-focused e-commerce services, said it has agreed to take over its competitor to form a new company that could be valued at nearly $3 billion, in the latest of a series of mergers and acquisitions in China's technology startup sector. The new company that brings together \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mogujie\f28 \uc2 \f2  and rival Meilishuo.com, which is backed by social network giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tencent Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  (0700.HK), will seek to raise fresh funds after completing the deal, Mogujie Chief Executive Chen Qi said in a letter to employees that was reviewed by The Wall Street Journal. Chen said in the letter that he would become the CEO of the new company. Tencent plans to increase its stake in the new company, a person familiar with the matter said. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mogujie\f28 \uc2 \f2 's deal with Meilishuo continues the streak of high-profile M&A deals among Chinese startups. As venture capitalists and other investors become more cautious about putting high price tags on companies that are burning through cash to compete with rivals, startups in China are under pressure to consider teaming up with rivals. (juro.osawa@wsj.com; @JuroOsawa) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0312 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] North Korea's sudden collapse would be a bigger threat to South Korea than an inter-Korean military conflict, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It forms this view even as risk of conflict grows following Pyongyang's fourth atomic bomb test last week. "A regime collapse in North Korea would likely lead to a disorderly reunification on the peninsula, weighing on South Korea's creditworthiness," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says in a note. Such a development would generate "acute financial strain" for South Korea. Parliament in Seoul estimates such a disorderly reunification would cost South Korea an annual average of 3.9% of gross domestic product for 45 years and also push Seoul's national debt up to 134% of GDP by 2040 versus 85% if the two Koreas were to remain divided. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says the status quo will likely prevail in the region because it expects the U.S. and China to contain the risk of an inter-Korean armed conflict. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese energy consumption last October and November grew at its slowest pace since the financial crisis. "China Electricity Consumption Lowest Since Financial Crisis -- Market Talk," at 0250 GMT, incorrectly said in the headline that electricity consumption had grown at its slowest pace since the financial crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0301 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Hong Kong dollar hit the weakest point in 10 months, reflecting fund outflows from the territory where stocks are falling alongside Chinese equities. The USD/HKD was as high as 7.7648 late Friday in New York and is still hovering at 7.7613 Monday morning--the weakest level since March 2015 and a big jump from 7.7530 area earlier Friday in Asia trading hours. "It's possibly a sign that money is flowing out of Hong Kong, given U.S. rates are on an upward trend," providing a better investment option for fast money, a senior trader at a local bank in Hong Kong says. It's a stark contrast from August, when \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar strengthened--triggering the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend the dollar peg--as local residents shifted their yuan investments to Hong Kong dollar amid sharp depreciation of the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "But funds parking in Hong Kong now don't find anything good to invest in," he says. (fiona.law@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0258 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/PHP is higher early Monday, getting a lift from strong U.S. nonfarm payrolls data that provides the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  scope to continue raising short-term US interest rates. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair is up at 47.24 after closing Friday at 47.165, but off early high 47.35. "The dollar appears capped for now. Many banks are already long on the dollar," said a local bank trader. Volume is light. Trader expects the near-term trading range at 46.80-47.50. (Cris.Larano@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 10, 2016 23:35 ET (04:35 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160111ec1b000bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
