\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dollar Hits 10-mo. Low, Reflecting Fund Outflows: Traders -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 203 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2016\par 05:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0301 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Hong Kong dollar hit the weakest point in 10 months, reflecting fund outflows from the territory where stocks are falling alongside Chinese equities. The USD/HKD was as high as 7.7648 late Friday in New York and is still hovering at 7.7613 Monday morning--the weakest level since March 2015 and a big jump from 7.7530 area earlier Friday in Asia trading hours. "It's possibly a sign that money is flowing out of Hong Kong, given U.S. rates are on an upward trend," providing a better investment option for fast money, a senior trader at a local bank in Hong Kong says. It's a stark contrast from August, when \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar strengthened--triggering the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the dollar peg--as local residents shifted their yuan investments to Hong Kong dollar amid sharp depreciation of the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "But funds parking in Hong Kong now don't find anything good to invest in," he says. (fiona.law@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Editor: KLH\par \par \uc2 (Delayed by 1 hour)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 11-01-16 0417GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160111ec1b0003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
