\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2015\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: U.S. FIRMS URGE CHINA TO IMPROVE CONDITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. businesses are pushing Chinese authorities to improve legal transparency, market access and intellectual-property rights across industries from technology to pharmaceuticals after foreign companies faced a spate of new regulatory hurdles in the country recently. (published 0354 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SIGNALS READINESS FOR FURTHER RATE CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signals further interest rates cuts may be needed to help rebalance an economy that is struggling to grow following the end of a decade-long mining boom. (published 0130 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN GOVERNMENT TAPS YUKITOSHI FUNO AS NEW BOJ BOARD MEMBER -- PARLIAMENTARY OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Tuesday nominated a senior adviser to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . as a candidate to replace an outgoing \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  policy board member. (published 0237 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREAN PRIME MINISTER OFFERS TO RESIGN OVER BRIBERY ACCUSATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's prime minister late Monday offered to resign over a bribery accusation--after two months in office--marking a fresh setback for a government faced with falling public support. (published 0247 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DURING NEW YORK TRADE MONDAY TO KEEP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WITHIN TRADING BAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold US$1.195 billion worth of Hong Kong dollars to keep the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in its trading band during New York trade Monday, the de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0130 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA PUSHING MORE SOES TO ISSUE BONDS - UPDATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's plans to root out graft at huge state companies, lure investment from China and take control of its largest gas field (published 0447 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA HIRES PR AGENCY AHEAD OF ABE SPEECH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government has engaged a U.S. public relations firm to promote its position on Japan's war history ahead of a speech by Japanese Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Congress, an executive from the company said. (published 0242 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW CHINESE LAW POSES GROWING THREAT TO FOREIGN INVESTORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Major foreign companies and several Chinese Internet companies with U.S. stock-exchange listings are using a corporate structure in China in a way that may be rendered illegal under a proposed law. (published 0037 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING ENTERPRISES\f28 \uc2 \f2  UNIT PLANS TO ISSUE EURO-DENOMINATED BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing Enterprises Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to raise funds via a bond issuance through its wholly-owned unit in a bid to reduce debt and for working capital. (published 0426 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UNITED PHOTOVOLTAICS ISSUES US$15 MILLION CONVERTIBLE BONDS TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 FOSUN INTERNATIONAL\f28 \uc2 \f2 'S UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese photovoltaics power-plant operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Photovoltaics Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it is issuing US$15 million worth of convertible bonds to a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fosun International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0206 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 21, 2015 02:00 ET (06:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150421eb4l000fv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
