\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-China charge into HK stocks both boon and bane\b0\par\par\uc2 861 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2015\par 08:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects figure in second paragraph to 68 billion yuan, not $68 billion)\par \par \uc2 * Mainland inflows through stock connect programme flood HK\par \par \uc2 * Push \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  index to 7-year high\par \par \uc2 * Mainland retail investors seen more volatile\par \par \uc2 * Complicates management of liquidity, dollar peg\par \par \uc2 By Pete Sweeney and \uc2 Michelle Chen\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI/HONG KONG, April 16 (Reuters) - Surging investment from mainland China has jolted Hong Kong's stock market from the doldrums, but the volatility of such flows, driven by an unfamiliar breed of investor, presents new risks to the stability of the city's economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A Reuters analysis shows that Chinese investors have moved a net 68 billion yuan ($10.97 billion) into Hong Kong-listed stocks via the Shanghai-Hong Kong stock connect programme since its launch in November, the vast bulk of it during just a few days in April.\par \par \uc2 That new money, plus tens of billions of dollars from a separate channel for Chinese institutional investors and untold flows from Chinese-controlled offshore funds, has helped push the market's capitalisation to HK$28.6 trillion ($3.7 trillion) in April from HK$25.5 trillion in November.\par \par \uc2 That is driving profits in Hong Kong's financial industry, presenting opportunities for companies to raise capital and perhaps boosting consumer confidence.\par \par \uc2 But this tide of cash can flow out as quickly as it flowed in, especially if investors conclude the rally has run too far ahead of the slowing economies on both sides of the border.\par \par \uc2 "With the help of China's opening up, Hong Kong's status as a global financial centre has been enhanced. However, its economy is also entering into a bubble cycle, and it's just the beginning," said Raymond Yeung, analyst at ANZ in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 The Shanghai Composite Index has gained over 70 percent since late November when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a surprise cut to interest rates, and the rally began overflowing into Hong Kong stocks in April, pushing the \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  index up more than 11 percent so far this month to a seven-year high.\par \par \uc2 "(Inflows) will add pressure to the already high property prices and cause inflation," said Yeung. "It will also bring more risks when sudden capital outflows happen."\par \par \uc2 According to exchange data, 62 percent of mainland Chinese investors in Hong Kong in 2014 were ordinary retail investors, who tend to behave very differently to the institutional fund managers Hong Kong is accustomed to.\par \par \uc2 On average, domestic Chinese investors hold a stock for as little as 24 days, compared with 260 days in Hong Kong, \uc2 UBS\uc2  analyst Lu Wenjie said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 "These two groups of investors are totally different, and there will be certain chemical reactions as they meet," wrote Charles Li, CEO of the Hong Kong exchange (HKEx), on his blog.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  PEG\par \par \uc2 HKEx data for 2014 shows mainland investors made up only 5.1 percent of its total cash market trading by value, lagging institutional funds from the UK and United States, which together accounted for over 20 percent.\par \par \uc2 But that equation is changing rapidly.\par \par \uc2 The stock connect scheme means Chinese investors can invest up to 250 billion yuan ($40.3 billion) in Hong Kong markets, and that quota is expected to be widened this year. And the Chinese flows are amplified by foreign money riding on its coat tails.\par \par \uc2 All of which has pushed volatility in the Hong Kong and Shanghai bourses to record highs, producing wide price swings.\par \par \uc2 The potential for vast and sudden moves of liquidity in and out of the Hong Kong dollar will also complicate monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong operates one of the world's last remaining \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs to the U.S. dollar, which means it must buy or sell dollars when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks set to exceed its daily trading band.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  multiple times as demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars spiked.\par \par \uc2 "Invariably the investment opportunity at any one time will be on one side or the other, and this is likely to create sudden inflows and outflows that will put pressure on the Hong Kong dollar peg," said Francois Perrin, head of Greater China Equities for BNP Investment Partners.\par \par \uc2 Two individuals familiar with the exchange's thinking said Hong Kong, not Beijing, had originally requested the imposition of quotas for the programme for fear an exodus of capital into China could put pressure on the exchange's trading system and the dollar peg.\par \par \uc2 HKEx said the quotas "were mutually agreed between the regulators and the exchanges as a means of managing risk in the initial stages".\par \par \uc2 HKMA declined to directly answer questions related to the impact these flows might have on monetary strategy, but reiterated its policy to "monitor the market developments closely and maintain the stability of the Hong Kong dollar". ($1 = 7.7504 Hong Kong dollars) ($1 = 6.2037 Chinese yuan renminbi) ($1 = 6.1977 Chinese yuan renminbi) (Additional reporting by Samuel Shen in SHANGHAI, Michelle Price and Saikat Chatterjee in HONG KONG; Editing by Will Waterman) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-16T07:30:28.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150416eb4g002s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
