\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : Euro Falls To 3-week Low After Strong Jobless Claims\b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2015\par 22:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Joseph Adinolfi, MarketWatch , Tatsuo Ito\par \par \uc2 Analysts say Wednesday's Fed minutes are driving dollar's strength\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (MarketWatch) -- The euro fell Thursday to its lowest level against the dollar in three weeks after a strong jobless-claims report.\par \par \uc2 The euro (EURUSD) fell to $1.0656, its lowest level since March 19. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at $1.0780 Wednesday evening.\par \par \uc2 The Labor Department said that jobless claims climbed to a seasonally adjusted 281,000 last week, from a revised 267,000 the week before. The four-week average of jobless claims, meanwhile, dropped by 3,000 to 282,250, its lowest level since June 2000. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/jobless-claims-turn-higher-one-week-after-matching-15-year-low-2015-04-09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/jobless-claims-turn-higher-one-week-after-matching-15-year-low-2015-04-09}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 While this morning's data was strong, analysts said that the minutes from a March meeting of \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  policy makers represented the largest driver of the dollar's rally.\par \par \uc2 The minutes, released Wednesday, showed that several policy makers had advocated raising the fed-funds rate at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's June meeting, causing traders to push the dollar higher on the expectation that a June rate hike was still on the table.\par \par \uc2 "There's a higher probability that they go earlier than what the market is pricing in," said Aroop Chatterjee, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , referring to the timing of what would be the first increase in the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's benchmark interest rate since 2006.\par \par \uc2 Comments from New York Fed President \uc2 William Dudley\uc2 , made Wednesday, supported the notion that a June interest-rate increase remains a possibility.\par \par \uc2 The buck (USDJPY) traded at 120.61 yen, compared with Yen120.15 Wednesday. The pound (GBPUSD) traded at $1.4710, compared with $1.4874 Wednesday, after the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  made no changes to monetary policy at its meeting Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Read: \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  keeps key rate at record low 0.5% ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/bank-of-england-keeps-key-rate-at-record-low-05-2015-04-09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/bank-of-england-keeps-key-rate-at-record-low-05-2015-04-09}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Several analysts played down the significance of the minutes, arguing that supposedly "data dependent" policy makers may have had a change of heart after Friday's surprisingly weak nonfarm payrolls report.\par \par \uc2 "Of course we should not forget the minutes came ahead of the most recent NFP disappointment, so 'several' members may longer be an appropriate estimate of Fed sensibilities. We can also debate what 'several' actually means. With 10 voting on rates in March we can assume it's not more than five and it's above a couple," said Jeremy Stretch, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce\uc2 , in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  news, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling $400 million-worth of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the Hong Kong dollar within a trading band set by monetary policy makers, according to Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar (USDHKD) traded at 7.7501 to the dollar Thursday, little-changed from a day ago.\par \par \uc2 Read: \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its dollar ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/hong-kong-monetary-authority-intervenes-to-weaken-its-dollar-2015-04-09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/\b  \highlight22hong-kong\b0 \highlight22 -\b  \highlight22monetary-authority\b0 \highlight22 -\b  \highlight22intervenes\b0 \highlight22 -to-weaken-its-dollar-2015-04-09}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The ICE U.S. Dollar Index (DXY), a measure of the dollar's strength against a basket of six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose 1% to 98.9110.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 09, 2015 16:21 ET (20:21 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150409eb49003iw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
