\par\par \b \uc2 *HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Keep  \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong \highlight\uc2  Dollar Within Trading Band\b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2015\par 13:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 9 Apr 2015 07:09 ET *HKMA Bought US$400 Mln From \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market As Hong Kong Dollar Strengthens To Hit Band\par \par \uc2 9 Apr 2015 07:34 ET  HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  To Keep \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Dollar Within Trading Band\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Fiona Law \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HONG KONG--The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the city's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sold US$400 million equivalent of Hong Kong dollars to keep the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in its trading band.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong dollar has strengthened in recent days as local stocks have jumped sharply. It was the first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the HKMA since July last year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is allowed to trade between HK$7.75-HK$7.85 against the greenback. Under the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to buy or sell the Hong Kong unit when it hits either side of its trading band.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Fiona Law at Fiona.Law@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 09, 2015 07:34 ET (11:34 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150409eb49001ai\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picsca