\par\par \b \uc2 India Shares Recover After \uc2 S&P\uc2  Raises Outlook to Stable -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2014\par 11:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0945 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Indian shares recover after \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  revises the country's outlook to stable from negative. The \uc2 S&P\uc2  BSE Sensex is up 0.7% to 26664.51 points. It fell as much as 0.9% in early trade. "India's improved political setting heralds a more conducive environment for reforms, providing a boost to growth prospects and the potential for improved fiscal management," the ratings agency says. India's economy has struggled in recent years due to slowing growth and rising inflation as a slow pace of policy changes, poor infrastructure and bureaucratic red-tape hurt investor confidence. A revival in metal stocks after two days of losses following the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  verdict on coal mining licenses also boosts the market sentiment. Among major gainers on the Sensex, Hindalco (500440.BY) rises 4%, \uc2 Axis Bank\uc2  (532215.BY) gains 3.2%, while \uc2 Tata Steel\uc2  (500470.BY) is trading up 2.7%. (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0000 GMT (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--Strength in the December Bund future is likely to meet considerable resistance at the nearby 149.85/149.91 highs. The uptrend this week has created an upside gap at 149.48, extending the recovery from the September 19 bear failure low at 147.63 that has the August 28 contract high at 149.91 within range. The close proximity to the 150 level, and also the 149.85 peak marked on the Equalized Active continuation chart, highlights the importance bears give to the area, and a clean break above 149.85/150 would open the upper half of the 151.83/147.63 decline on the standard continuation chart. Room for 150.49 would then be opened. The Market Profile charts this week indicate strong support at 149.11/149.17. The December Bund future is at 149.61.\par \par \uc2 Market Profile is an intraday charting technique, seeking to evaluate market value as it develops during the day. The technique displays price on a vertical axis, and time/activity on a horizontal axis, creating bell curves that show normal and variable distributions in financial markets.\par \par \uc2 -By Francis Bray, \uc2 Dow Jones Chief Technical\uc2  Analyst For Europe.\par \par \uc2 (francis.bray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 0924 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Malaysia won't impose a goods and services tax (GST) on investments in precious metals when the tax goes into effect next April, according to the president of the nation's Federation of Goldsmiths and Jewellers Association. "We were verbally told this at a closed door meeting with the deputy finance minister," said Ermin Siow. An official announcement is expected in early October. The industry considers precious metals to be similar to bonds and the stock market. "People invest in precious metals and hope for capital appreciation," said Louis Ng, executive chairman of Public Gold Group, adding that, in Malaysia, gold and silver were most popular. "If you want Malaysia to be the hub for trading of precious metals, than there must be no GST." (celine.fernandez@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0917 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The vast amount of funds that flowed into Hong Kong in July has been quietly exiting the territory, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daiwa\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Data show net inflows of $19 billion into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in July-August, triggering dozens of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep a burgeoning Hong Kong dollar within its trading band, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daiwa\f28 \uc2 \f2 . But when there are outflows, the HKMA doesn't need to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as long as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar stays in the trading band. "This has likely been the case in the past few weeks. In other words, money has quietly left Hong Kong without anyone noticing," the house says in a report. It adds that the many headlines over the summer about HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were hyped by the media, which has had less interest in the outflow story. The Hong Kong dollar is allowed to trade between 7.75-7.85 to the US dollar. (fiona.law@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0851 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Conference Board\f28 \uc2 \f2  said its Leading Economic Index for China increased 0.7% in August decelerating from a 1.2% increase in July and a 1.3% rise in June. The group's Coincident Economic Index, meanwhile, remained unchanged in August following a 1.0% increase in both July and June. "The monthly growth in the LEI for China slowed markedly in August as real estate activity weakened and consumer expectations fell again," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Conference Board\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Andrew Polk\f28 \uc2 \f2 . While targeted stimulus may provide some support in the fourth quarter, "the LEI does not point to a sustained pick up in the economy any time soon," he added. (mark.magnier@WSJ.com; and on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2  @MarkMagnier) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0847 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  lowers its 2015 GDP growth estimate to 4.8% from an earlier projection of 5.5% as it believes "the slow merchandise export and tourism recoveries are projected to continue into 2015 and contribute to lower growth outlook for the year". BOT also cut its export growth forecast to 4.0% from 6.0%. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  affirms its stance that "the current degree of monetary policy accommodation is still needed to support economic recovery". BOT maintained the benchmark policy interest rate at 2.0% for four consecutive meetings. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0840 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The vote by the Indonesian parliament to end direct regional elections is indicative of President-elect Joko Widodo's precarious reform agenda, says Nomura. Under the new law, members of the local house of representatives will decide on the mayors, regents and governors, who will no longer be elected directly by the people. The Merah Putih coalition--led by Prabowo Subianto, who ran in the presidential elections against Widodo--pushed through the election law. President-elect Widodo still does not have a majority in the incoming parliament and relies on the coalition to stay in office. "This does not bode well for reform prospects, and shows how determined the Merah Putih coalition is," says Nomura. In the near term, this increases concerns over whether Jokowi can cut subsidies as soon as November as stated by Widodo's advisers recently. "We maintain our baseline view of no fuel price hikes this year," Nomura adds. (I-made.sentana@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0837 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China government bonds are steady as investors remain cautious ahead of a long holiday. The five-year government bond yield is one basis point higher at 3.93%, the seven-day government bond yield is unchanged at 3.99%. China's financial markets will be closed from October 1-7 for public holiday. Liquidity remains ample, despite rising cash demand ahead of holiday. The benchmark seven-day repo rate is down to 3.30% versus 3.42% late Thursday. "There is so much money in the market, it doesn't feel then the end of the third quarter and before the national holiday at all," says a Shanghai-based trader at a Chinese bank. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0835 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 US Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields dip below 2.50% in London, hitting their lowest levels in a couple of weeks, as the risk-off bid remains firm on economic concerns, heightened conflict in Iraq and talk of a potential foreign asset grab by Russia. All eyes will be on the 2Q U.S. GDP release at 1230 GMT with expectations that the already-strong US Q2 GDP reading will be revised up to a gain of 4.6% q/q saar, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2 . December \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  futures are 5/32 higher at 124-290 and the 10s yield 2.492%. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0833 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/TWD is little changed as exporter sales help offset foreign fund outflows, say two local traders. The pair closes at 30.312 vs 30.310 late Thursday; they say the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is believed to have bought the USD around 30.280 (vs 30.290 Thursday) to keep the pair in its target band. "Exporter will likely be more eager to sell [the USD] on Monday as the month-end approaches, so the USD/TWD is unlikely to advance too much," a trader says, and tips the pair to trade between 30.270 and 30.320 Monday. The Taiex ends 0.2% lower Friday. Foreign investors have been net sellers of local stocks for 13 straight sessions. (fanny.liu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0832 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects government bond issuance in the eurozone to amount EUR25 billion next week, exceeding the year-to-date average of around EUR19.5 billion. Next week's scheduled issuers are Italy with up to EUR8.5 billion Monday, followed by Germany's EUR5 billion Wednesday. Spain and France auction bonds Thursday, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  expecting EUR7.5-EUR8.5 billion from France and EUR3-EUR4 billion from Spain. The French Treasury Agency announces terms of next week's auctions at 0900 GMT. The Spanish Treasury announces details of the auction in two steps: it picks the bonds on Friday and announces the target volume Monday. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 26 Sep 2014 05:45 ET \par India Shares Recover After \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  Raises Outlook to -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0827 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]---Before selling a considerable amount of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to commercial banks operating in Hungary so that they could convert households' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loans at an unspecified date into HUF, Hungary is bolstering its foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Hungarian state-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 --Eximbank--has just issued $500 million in a USD bond, which was more than four times over-subscribed, and part of an EUR2-billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond issuance program launched in 2012. "We see this as continuation of the government's push to bolster the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves as far as possible before it writes down these reserves during the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mortgage loan swap next year," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 26, 2014 05:45 ET (09:45 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140926ea9q000wy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
