\par\par \b \uc2 *HKMA Injects HK$7.169 Bln to Defend US Dollar Peg Monday\b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2014\par 03:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 4 Aug 2014 21:27 ET  HKMA Injects HK$7.169 Bln to Defend US Dollar Peg Monday\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Chester Yung \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--The \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday injects HK$7.169 billion (US$925 million) into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transaction data from the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was triggered by the U.S. dollar hitting HK$7.7500, the strong side of the Hong Kong dollar's trading band.\par \par \uc2 At 0108 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at HK$7.7502, steady from late Monday.\par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggregate balance--a measurement of the city's interbank liquidity--to HK$238.025 billion.\par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is pegged at HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar but is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85. The HKMA is obliged to buy or sell the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it touches either side of that band.\par \par \uc2 Write to Chester Yung at chester.yung@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 04, 2014 21:27 ET (01:27 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140805ea850003r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
