\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong \highlight\uc2  Ramps Up  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  to Curb Local  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  -3-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Fiona Law   \par \uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2014\par 12:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected $65.1 billion Hong Kong dollars (US$8.4 billion) into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in July to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the U.S. dollar as foreign funds continued to pour into the city to feed a hunger for Chinese assets.\par \par \uc2 Funds have been flowing into Hong Kong, which offers foreigners an easy way to tap Chinese stocks and bonds, at a faster pace than late 2012, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors' risk appetite for the city's stocks rose.\par \par \uc2 At that time, HKMA injected HK$107 billion (US$13.8 billion) into the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from October to December in a bid to cool the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  totaled more than half that amount in the span of a single month.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA--obliged to buy or sell the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it touches either side of the authority's HK$7.75-HK$7.85 band against the U.S. dollar--said Saturday that it attributed the strength of the Hong Kong dollar to listed companies' dividend payments, cross-border merger-and-acquisition deals such as \uc2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp\uc2 .'s HK$40 billion takeover of \uc2 Wing Hang Bank Ltd\uc2 ., as well as an active market for initial public offerings.\par \par \uc2 In July, the benchmark \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  Index had its best month since 2012, posting a 6.8% gain and hitting a three-year high, as China's improving economy persuaded investors to snap up the city's stocks, which are made up mostly of mainland Chinese companies.\par \par \uc2 Russia's second-largest mobile operator, OAO MegaFon, has decided to keep about 40% of its cash reserves in Hong Kong dollars because of global market instability and as the West imposes sanctions on Moscow in a bid to force President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to end his support for separatist rebels in Ukraine, The Wall Street Journal reported this week.\par \par \uc2 The fact that China's \uc2 Huawei Technologies Co\uc2 . is its main equipment manufacturer was another factor in MegaFon's decision, according to the report.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Hong Kong dollar remained sticky at the strong end of its trading band--HK$7.75 per dollar--and analysts have said they expect it to stay elevated as a program that allows direct trading between Hong Kong and Shanghai shares was likely to stoke demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "But funds do not flow in one direction only," \uc2 Peter Pang\uc2 , HKMA's deputy chief executive, said Saturday. "Last year's market turmoil caused by a large-scale outflow of funds from certain emerging markets showed that the direction of fund flows could change spontaneously in response to investors' sentiments."\par \par \uc2 "As the U.S. economy recovers and its monetary environment normalizes, there remain considerable uncertainties in the future direction of fund flows," Mr. Pang said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Fiona Law at fiona.law@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 01-08-14 1048GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140801ea810007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
