\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong shares rise on strong telecoms, China lifted by carmakers\b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2014\par 06:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * HSI +0.4 pct, H-shares +0.4 pct, CSI300 +0.3 pct               \par \par \uc2 * China's 3 largest carriers rise after deal on telecoms-tower firm               \par \par \uc2 * Auto sector strong again as govt encourages 'green' cars               \par \par \uc2 * Macau casinos weaker amid graft probe into a land deal   (Updates to midday)               \par \par \uc2 By Grace Li               \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, July 14 (Reuters) - Hong Kong shares rose on Monday with China's three state-owned wireless carriers leading gains, while mainland markets were also stronger as auto stocks extended their advance on new policy support.               \par \par \uc2 At midday, the CSI300 of the leading Shanghai and Shenzhen A-share listings climbed 0.3 percent, while the Shanghai Composite Index was up 0.4 percent at 2,054.83 points.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  Index and the \uc2 China Enterprises\uc2  Index  of the top Chinese listings in Hong Kong each added 0.4 percent. The benchmark index stood at 23,320.83 points, after earlier climbing above 23,450.               \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong benchmark has risen more than 7 percent since early May.               \par \par \uc2 Jackson Wong, vice-president of Tanrich Securities in Hong Kong, said inflows of funds over the weekend cheered the market. "That's a pretty good sentiment booster right now," he said.               \par \par \uc2 Analysts said one indication of hot money inflows is a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the city's peg to the U.S. dollar.               \par \par \uc2 On Friday alone, the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) sold HK$10.540 billion (US$1.36 billion) as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit the strong end of its trading range.               \par \par \uc2 On Monday, \uc2 China Unicom\uc2  climbed 3.4 percent, the top percentage gainer among \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  components, while China Mobile and \uc2 China Telecom\uc2  moved up 2.2 and 2.8 percent, respectively.               \par \par \uc2 The country's three largest telecoms said late on Friday they had agreed to jointly establish a telecommunications tower company with a registered capital of 10 billion yuan ($1.61 billion), which analysts said would cut their costs.               \par \par \uc2 China Communications Services\uc2 , a related equipment supplier, jumped 7.2 percent to a 2-1/2 month high.               \par \par \uc2 The auto sector was strong again after posting solid gains on Friday helped by a tax exemption on green cars.               \par \par \uc2 In a notice published on Sunday, China urged government officials to use more electric and plug-in hybrid cars as part of its drive to cut pollution. It aims to put 5 million such vehicles on the road by 2020.               \par \par \uc2 SAIC Motor Corp\uc2  rose 1.7 percent, following Friday's 1.6 percent, to its highest since Dec. 10. BYD  gained 3.7 percent in Hong Kong, leading H-share gains.               \par \par \uc2 Casinos were underperformers as a probe into a land deal relating to \uc2 Wynn Macau\uc2  by Macau's corruption agency hurt sentiment.               \par \par \uc2 Beijing is due to release its second-quarter growth figure on Wednesday. The pace is expected to hold firm at 7.4 percent and anything less than that would likely unsettle markets.               \par \par \uc2 Investors are also watching for June money supply and loan growth, due by Tuesday. Monthly urban investment, industrial output and retail sales figures are also expected on Wednesday.                              \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-7-14T05:55:21.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140714ea7e0020q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
