\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Stable After Weak 2Q GDP -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2014\par 07:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0515 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Singapore dollar is flat compared with its Monday opening of 1.2403 even after surprisingly weaker second-quarter gross domestic product data. It is currently at 1.2410 compared with the U.S. unit. USD/SGD has been bobbing above the round-figure trading barrier at 1.2400 for most of the day but remains in a bearish technical bias as long as the ceiling of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel is intact by Monday's closing. The channel could direct USD/SGD to the base of the weekly downtrend channel at 1.2369 in the days ahead. The Singapore dollar typically reacts more to external data from developed countries owing to the country's reliance on trade. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0504 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Indian rupee gains moderately versus the U.S. dollar, weighing USD/INR down and away from the Bollinger uptrend channel at 60.21. The daily chart suggests a technical range of 59.83-60.21 could trap USD/INR for the near term. If USD/INR breaks either end of this range, the daily Bollinger downtrend or uptrend channel will be activated respectively. The small movements in India's equity market as well as in other Asian stock markets suggests risk appetite is lean, giving \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  little fodder for volatility. USD/INR is now 59.99 from its Friday close of 60.08. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0452 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Indian shares open slightly lower Monday as confusion prevails over implementation of the General Anti-Avoidance Rules (GAAR). GAAR was proposed in the 2012-13 budget to prevent tax evaders operating through shadow companies in tax havens. Nirmala Sitharaman, minister of state for finance, said Friday the law would be applicable from April 1, 2015, while revenue secretary Shaktikanta Das said the Government is yet to take a view on introduction of this new law. The S&P BSE Sensex is down 0.1% at 25001.76 points, while the National Stock Exchange Nifty index also declines 0.1% at 7,453.30. Major losers on the Sensex are \uc2 Infosys\uc2 , \uc2 Bharti Airtel\uc2  and \uc2 Hindustan Unilever\uc2 . (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0444 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Hong Kong equities advance in early trading, putting the Hang Seng Index on track to extend a rally begun last week into a third day, with telecoms companies leading gains. The Hang Seng Index is up 0.4% to 23,320.83, with Chinese telecoms rising most after they announced the incorporation a jointly owned tower operator on Friday. \uc2 China Unicom\uc2  (0762.HK) tops the market with gains of 3.4% to HK$12.70, while China Mobile (0941.HK) is up 2.2% to HK$78.25 and \uc2 China Telecom\uc2  (0728.HK) rises 2.8% to HK$4.01, as casino stocks decline most. This afternoon's trading is unlikely to rattle Asia, with Europe likely to get off to a "slow start", says CMC Markets: "France are away celebrating National day, while some Germans are likely to self-declare one, with their fourth winning title at the World Cup." (gregor.hunter@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @gregorhunter)\par \par \uc2 0442 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The higher-than-expected uptick in India's industrial-production index in May could have lifted GDP growth in the second quarter to 5.2% year-on-year, Nomura says, which is above the bank's forecast of 4.7%. Helped by strong growth in the production of consumer goods, total factory output rose by 4.7% year-on-year in May compared with 3.4% in April, handily beating most expectations. Looking at the data another way, the picture is less rosy but still not bad. The index rose just 0.2% month-on-month on a seasonally adjusted basis, down from 1.8% in April. Nomura says it still expects 5% real GDP growth for the year ending March 2015. (raymond.zhong@wsj.com, \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @zhonggg)\par \par \uc2 0413 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Funds buying up the Hong Kong dollar are vying for Shanghai-Hong Kong cross-market stock investment program, \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  strategist Frances Cheung says. The USD/HKD has been weighed down and repeatedly hit 7.75--the lower band of the peg triggering \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sold a combined HK$37.12 billion (US$4.8 billion) in the past two weeks. "People are parking funds in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , waiting for buying opportunities when the Hong Kong-Shanghai Connect kickstarts," she says, attributing to China's trial program to allow cross-market stock trading between Hong Kong- and Shanghai-listed stocks, which is expected to be launched in the second half of 2014. The USD/HKD is still currently trading near 7.75. (fiona.law@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0403 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] China's shares tread higher but concerns over company earnings growth outlook might curb the upside, say analysts. The Shanghai Composite Index is up 0.45 at 2054.83 and is tipped to face immediate resistance at 2100. "The market is skittish" as investors weigh potential weakness in economic growth momentum against Premier Li Keqiang's pledges to stabilize economy, says Guotai Asset Management in a note. China is due to release major economic indicators, such as GDP for 2Q, on Wednesday. Auto makers lead gains in response to Beijing's move to boost the sector. Anhui Jianghua Automobile (600418.SH) rises by its 10% daily upside limit to CNY12.34 while Faw Car (000800.SZ) jumps 7.8% to CNY10.50. The Shenzhen Composite Index gains 0.4% to 1112.64.(amy.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0401 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 KKR & Co\uc2 . bought a 24.9% stake in Houston-based hedge-fund firm BlackGold Capital Management LP, according to people familiar with the deal, part of the private-equity firm's solidifying hedge-fund strategy. The deal with BlackGold, a roughly $1.4 billion, credit-oriented firm that invests in the natural-resources and energy space, closed Friday after about a year of talks, the people said. The deal comes amid an uptick in hedge-fund stakes buying, as investment firms have raised billions for partnerships they say can provide an attractive revenue stream. While \uc2 KKR\uc2  is using its balance sheet for such deals, industry experts say to expect more stakes deals. (juliet.chung@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0332 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] AUD/USD is currently hemmed in as low volatility accentuates the carry trade, while weak economic data is strengthening expectations of another interest rate cut, according to NAB. "The push versus pull of the low volatility, risk-on market against the signs of faltering in the domestic economy--which is allowing the fixed income market to price in easing ahead--means that the Australian dollar is stuck at present levels," NAB's Global Co-Head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategy, Ray Attrill says. "At current levels of vol, which are historically low, we may need to see a more sustained rise in market risk aversion before it reacts in the typically negative fashion." He recommends shorting AUD/USD on any spike higher.(david.rogers@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @DavidRogersWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0332 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Despite ongoing geo-political risk and the hunt for yield keeping bonds well bid, the NZD/USD continues to display extraordinary strength, says Annette Beacher, \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  head of Asia Pacific Research. At 0.882, the pair is not only ignoring local housing data released earlier but could test post-float highs this week if Fed Chair Yellen reiterates a dovish tone, she says. "The overall tone of the (housing) report felt heavy, with the REINZ (Real Estate Institute of New Zealand) reporting that many regions are flat-lining, and taking longer to sell what stock is on offer, with Auckland the standout hot spot." While senior RBNZ officials may prefer a lower \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and higher interest rates, the zero-cash global environment won't be delivering that combination any time soon, "and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk is futile," Beacher says. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com;\uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @lucy_craymer)\par \par \uc2 0320 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Australian house prices rebounded in the past week, with Sydney prices up 11.5% in annualized trend terms, according to \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2 . "Despite consumer confidence remaining only moderately higher than the recent post-Budget lows, home prices increased strongly in Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane in the past week," ANZ Senior Property Analyst David Cannington says. Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens said earlier this month that "investors should take care" in the Sydney property market after a large increase in borrowing and an increase in lending with high loan-to-value ratios in recent quarters. The Governor also said some segments of the housing market appear to have been calming down lately. (david.rogers@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @DavidRogersWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0310 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] China's value-added industrial production likely rose 9.0% in June, the median forecast from 19 economists surveyed by The Wall Street Journal. That would be slightly up from May's 8.8% increase. "Thanks to an accommodative policy environment...we expect June and 2Q's upcoming data to show an economy still in, albeit modest, recovery," \uc2 UBS\uc2  economists say in a note. The same survey also shows that fixed-asset investment in non-rural areas, a closely watched indicator of construction activity, likely climbed 17.2% on year in the first six months of the year, unchanged from the on-year increase in the January-May period. The data set is due at 0200 GMT Wednesday. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 14, 2014 01:15 ET (05:15 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140714ea7e0009c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
