\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong \highlight\uc2  Seen to Keep  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  to Cap the HKD: ING -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2014\par 07:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0405 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the HK dollar as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be higher, says ING. The HKMA on Tuesday injected cash into the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to cool down the local unit, which is pegged to the U.S. dollar within a range of HK$7.75 to HK$7.85 per dollar. "It was the first in what will prove to be another episode of concerted defense of the peg," says ING. The house believes the HKD's strength was due to better risk appetite amid improved sentiment towards China. Meanwhile, there's speculative USD selling vs HKD because of the USD's weakness against major \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and against the CNY at the end of June. ING expects sentiment towards China to continue to pick up, which in turn will "persist confidence-sensitive inflows into Hong Kong to force the HKMA into another sustained defense of 7.75," it says. The USD/HKD is still hovering around 7.7507 Friday. (fiona.law@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (Delayed by 1 hour)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 04-07-14 0548GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140704ea740003k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
