\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong offshore yuan deposits seen extending October's rapid rise\b0\par\par\uc2 By Saikat Chatterjee and Michelle Chen   \par \uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2013\par 05:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Dec 2 (Reuters) - A wide gap in the price of the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in offshore and  onshore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets suggests that a jump in offshore yuan deposits with Hong Kong banks in October may be repeated in November.\par \par \uc2 Yuan deposits with Hong Kong banks rose by their biggest margin in the month of October since April 2011, the latest data from the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the city's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed.\par \par \uc2 Deposits rose 52 billion yuan ($8.5 billion) to 781.6 billion yuan in October compared to a month earlier, the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a monthly report published on its website. Related chart: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/geh67t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/geh67t}}}\par \par \uc2 "The widening price differential between the onshore and the offshore yuan attracted a lot of yuan buyers in the Hong Kong market, resulting in an increase in the deposit base," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at a Chinese Bank in Hong Kong who declined to be identified.\par \par \uc2 While the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Hong Kong market and on the mainland have traded virtually in lock-step with each other for most of this year, it started to diverge noticeably since September when the offshore yuan or CNH as it is popularly known started trading at a premium to the onshore rate.\par \par \uc2 That was driven by Beijing's resolve to keep a tight grip on the yuan's rise which has been easily the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia this year with a gain of more than 2 percent against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Onshore yuan rose 0.45 percent in October while the offshore yuan rose 0.6 percent in that period.\par \par \uc2 As state-run banks stepped up their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the onshore market in a tight range, likely on the behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , large companies betting on more yuan gains took to buying the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Hong Kong market, opening up a gap for the first time since January.\par \par \uc2 "The October statistics could suggest that yuan flows between mainland China and Hong Kong have been skewed more towards flows into Hong Kong, likely on renewed expectations on yuan appreciation," said Frances Cheung, a strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 The gap between the offshore and the onshore yuan hit a high of 149 pips on Oct. 4 and widened to more to 300 pips on Nov. 19 before pulling back somewhat, suggesting that CNH deposits in November may see yet another sharp jump.\par \par \uc2 Notwithstanding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the heavy outright dollar selling in the mainland in October sparked the speculation of renewed yuan gains and triggered demand for yuan-denominated assets.\par \par \uc2 At a Nov. 21 auction for a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  yuan-denominated bond in Hong Kong, yields for the three-year tranche was priced at 2.6 percent, a new record low and far below 2.87 percent in June for a similar maturity.\par \par \uc2 Data released last month showed \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commercial banks purchased 441.6 billion yuan ($72.49 billion) worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a net basis in October, indicating China saw increased net capital inflows in October. Chart: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/pev95t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/pev95t}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined comment.   (Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 CHINA-YIAN/DEPOSITS | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | Z | ABX | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131202e9c20004u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
