\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA defends Hong Kong dollar peg, selling HK$5 bln\b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2012\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Dec 21 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, selling HK$5.038 billion ($650 million) in Hong Kong dollars as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly hit the strong end of its trading range.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters data, the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lift the aggregate balance - the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA - to HK$255.85 billion on Dec. 27.\par \par \uc2 The cumulative amount of Hong Kong dollars injected into the market since Oct. 20 is $13.831 billion.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 7.7500 against the U.S. dollar at 0914 GMT. ($1 = 7.7500 Hong Kong dollars)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Michelle Chen; Editing by Lee Chyen Yee)\par \par \uc2 HONGKONG-HKMA/ (URGENT) | ABX | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121221e8cl000ga\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
