\par\par \b \uc2 Yen and Dollar Sink Ahead of FOMC Meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 798 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2012\par 13:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Japanese yen hits 8-month low against dollar ahead of weekend elections\par \par \uc2 -- Australian, New Zealand and Canadian dollars gain against buck as FOMC looms\par \par \uc2 -- \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells Hong Kong dollars to protect peg\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Alexandra Fletcher \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen weakened against the dollar and euro in European trading at the prospect of looser monetary policy in Japan after elections there Sunday, while the dollar fell against most other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's latest update.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar rose to its highest level in more than eight months against the yen, peaking at Y82.94 early in the session. The euro popped above Y108 for the first time since April 5, helped by a sharp tightening in Greek bond yields.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Media polls in Japan have shown that the main opposition Liberal Democratic Party, led by former premier Shinzo Abe, is on its way to a sweeping victory that could hand it and its smaller ally a key two-thirds majority. The leader of the center-right LDP has promised to boost public spending and has called for unlimited easing by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  to achieve 2% inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is obviously plenty of event risk going into the weekend," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ian Stannard\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London. "The dollar could go to Y84.00 against the yen if monetary policy expands post-elections."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aside from against the yen, the dollar was also broadly weaker as market participants looked ahead to the Federal Open Market Committee's statement at 1730 GMT. With \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Twist drawing to a close, the Fed is expected to announce another stimulus program in the form of outright purchases of U.S. Treasuries worth $45 billion a month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commodity-linked \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the Australian, New Zealand and Canadian dollars were the main benefactors of dollar weakness, climbing to a series of multi-month highs, while the euro rose further above $1.30 against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Although the view that the Fed will shift to outright Treasury purchases is now very widely shared by market participants, we do not believe it has been fully reflected into markets or in positioning. Hence, further dollar weakness is highly likely should the Fed shift," said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold HK$4.65 billion ($600 million) to prevent the Hong Kong dollar from strengthening beyond its peg to the U.S. dollar. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was triggered by the U.S. dollar hitting HK$7.7500, the strong side of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's trading band. The latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increases \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's aggregate balance--a measurement of the city's interbank liquidity--to HK$225.0 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking ahead, Fed Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ben Bernanke\f28 \uc2 \f2  is also due to hold a press conference at around 1915 GMT, and the U.S. monthly budget statement is due at 1900 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1145 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.3028 against the dollar, compared with $1.3006 late Tuesday in New York, according to trading system EBS. The dollar was at Y82.84 against the yen, compared with Y82.51, while the euro was at Y107.91, compared with Y107.30.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pound was trading at $1.6146 against the dollar, compared with $1.6114 late Tuesday in New York. The Wall Street Journal dollar index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 70.145 from about 70.185.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below:\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1139 GMT     1.3028     82.84      1.6142     0.9304 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish    Bullish    Bullish    Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bearish    Bullish    Range      Bullish \par 200 day ma        1.2880     79.69      1.5905     0.9383 \par 3rd Resistance    1.3172     83.39      1.6271     0.9383 \par 2nd Resistance    1.3127     83.31      1.6217     0.9370 \par 1st Resistance    1.3070     83.00      1.6175     0.9325 \par Pivot*            1.2983     82.46      1.6102     0.9337 \par 1st Support       1.2977     82.55      1.6096     0.9295 \par 2nd Support       1.2945     82.30      1.6061     0.9241 \par 3rd Support       1.2921     82.11      1.6041     0.9215 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/JPY \par  \par Spot 1139 GMT     107.91 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish \par 200 day ma        102.65 \par 3rd Resistance    108.66 \par 2nd Resistance    108.33 \par 1st Re